# For and against in Russian: против, ради, среди
subtitle: "Say you are for or against, for whose sake and among whom in Russian: я про́тив, ра́ди дете́й, среди́ сосе́дей, at a debate about cars and trees."
tags: ["russian","for and against","против ради среди","debate in russian","russian phrases"]
teaches: ["phrases/debating","phrases/arguing","grammar/verb-cases"]
thumb: "band \"For or against in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Reading Kuprin in Russian: The Elephant","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/190-russian-kuprin-elephant.cast"}

